  98: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  99:     """
 100:     Replicate a pre-drawn corner pattern to every other marker-bearing corner.
 101: 
 102:     Input structure:
 103:     - bg = most frequent color. Hollow 0-frames (possibly partial L-shapes); each
 104:       frame-corner cell is either 0 or a painted (non-bg, non-0) color.
 105:     - >= 1 'source' corner: the pattern is already drawn (one color, both outward
 106:       cells and an inward-diagonal trail).
 107:     - Other corners: a single colored pixel on the inward diagonal at the pattern's
 108:       deepest (k,k) offset; the pixel's color is that corner's target color.
 109: 
 110:     Rule:
 111:     - Extract the canonical (TL-oriented) pattern from any source.
 112:     - For each non-source corner whose marker cell is colored, paint the same
 113:       pattern rotated to that corner's orientation, using the marker's color.
 114: 
 115:     Key insight: the pattern is symmetric about the corner's inward-diagonal axis
 116:     (canonical dr == dc), so it reflects cleanly across all four corner orientations.
 117:     Painting uses each target's OWN marker color, not the source color.
 118:     """
